<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Town Demographics and Language Preferences</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>In a town of {@total_persons@} persons, {@read_hindi@} persons read Hindi, {@read_english@} read English and {@read_both@} read both.</p>
<p> Find the number of persons who read neither Hindi nor English</p>
<p>\(\quad\) [[input:ans1]][[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>To find the number of persons who read neither Hindi nor English, we can use the principle of inclusion-exclusion.</p>

<p>Let \(A\) be the set of persons who read Hindi, and \(B\) be the set of persons who read English. We are given that \(|A| = {@read_hindi@}\), \(|B| = {@read_english@}\), and \(|A \cap B| = {@read_both@}\).</p>

<p>Using the principle of inclusion-exclusion, we have:</p>
<p>\[ \displaystyle 
\begin{align}
|A \cup B| &= |A| + |B| - |A \cap B| \\
                  &= {@read_hindi@} + {@read_english@} - {@read_both@} \\
                 &={@persons_either_hindi_or_english@}
\end{align}\]</p>
<p>So, \({@persons_either_hindi_or_english@}\) persons read either Hindi or English or both.</p>

<p>Since there are \({@total_persons@}\) persons in total, the number of persons who read neither Hindi nor English is given by:</p>
<p>\[ \displaystyle 
\begin{align}
| \text{Neither Hindi nor English} | &= {@total_persons@} - |A \cup B| \\
                  &= {@total_persons@} - {@persons_either_hindi_or_english@} \\
                 &={@persons_neither_hindi_nor_english@}
\end{align}\]</p>
<p>Thus, \({@ta@}\) persons read neither Hindi nor English.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
